  "description": "Dual motors, each 1500W rated, with a combined 7200W peak output and up to 350 Nm torque, paired with Shimano 7-Speed gearing. Factory-set to Class 2 (20 mph), unlockable up to 44~50 mph, supporting Class 1, 2, 3, and off-road modes.\n\nLike two bikes in one, the Sensor Switch lets you choose between Torque or Cadence sensors, while the easy-to-read color display shows speed, battery level, and riding modes, giving you full control and a customized ride.\n\nFeaturing a lockable dual-shoulder front fork with a thru-axle, a DNM rear shock beneath the seat, and an additional suspension unit connecting the rear rack, this triple-suspension system effectively absorbs impacts, delivering enhanced comfort and stability on rough terrain and long-distance rides.\n\nEquipped with 60V 25Ah Samsung 50S 21700 high-discharge lithium-ion batteries (each with its own charger), the AndSky e-bike delivers an impressive 60–100 miles of range per charge when using PAS level 1 in Class 2 mode, with removable batteries for convenient charging and long-lasting, efficient performance.\n\nChoose between torque or cadence sensing, allowing the motor to respond either to your pedaling force for a more natural and efficient ride, or to your pedaling rhythm for smooth and consistent power assistance.\n\nEquipped with an EXSHO dual crown front fork with 70 mm of travel, adjustable for softness and rebound, and aluminum alloy fenders; the headlight features left/right turn signals, low beam, and high beam for safe riding day or night.\n\nWith 4-piston Gemma hydraulic brakes and 203mm rotors, you can rely on powerful, precise stopping performance, and the Innova 26×4 fat tires provide puncture-resistant traction for confident riding on any terrain.\n\nMade with extra-wide 11in design and high-resilience padding, it provides maximum comfort and effectively absorbs shocks from rough terrain, making it perfect for long-distance rides.\n\nDesigned for comfort, with pressure-relieving bubble zones in key areas that support your wrists and help prevent tendon strain. Keeps your hands naturally relaxed and reduces fatigue on long rides. The handlebar ends feature pre-drilled holes, allowing you to easily install rearview mirrors for added safety.\n\nEquipped with a rear light featuring left/right turn signals and a brake light, enhancing your visibility and safety on the road.",
